# 10. Add a financial reconciliation check

Every simulated plan should satisfy accounting invariants.

## Cash conservation

`EndingCash = StartingCash + RecordedCashInflows − RecordedCashOutflows`

## Liability conservation

`EndingOutstanding = InitialOutstanding + NewObligationsDue + Fees − Payments − Credits`

Use appropriate separation between cash-funded bill payments and restricted assistance.

## Wage reconciliation

`DirectRecoveredShifts + IndirectRecoveredShifts = TotalRecoveredShifts`

`DirectEarnedWages + IndirectEarnedWages = TotalRecoveredEarningPotential`

`PayrollReceivedWithinHorizon + PayrollPayableAfterHorizon = TotalApplicableEarnedPayroll`

Handle earnings outside the observation window carefully.

## Expense reconciliation

`TransitExpense = Sum(actual transit trips × applicable fare)`

No duplicated transit costs.

No transit costs when the shift was worked remotely or the repaired car was used instead.

## Bill reconciliation

`AmountDue = AmountPaid + AmountOutstanding`

At every relevant date.

No negative outstanding balances.

No cash spent twice.

### Assertions and diagnostics

Add internal validation checks where practical.

If a reconciliation fails, expose a developer diagnostic or reject the inconsistent plan instead of quietly presenting contradictory numbers.

