# 13. Tests and acceptance

## Base accounting

- Starting cash is reconciled with actual cash inflows/outflows.
- Negative theoretical balance doesn't imply a real overdraft.
- Unpaid bills create outstanding liabilities.
- Later payments reduce liabilities.
- Bills aren't paid twice.
- Outstanding balances never become negative.

## Timing

- Wage earnings and payroll deposits remain separate.
- Following-Friday delay remains correct.
- Bills due before payday cannot use later payroll.
- Repair is charged once.
- Repair cannot retroactively restore an earlier shift.

## Expenses

- Historical recurring expenses aren't double-counted with scheduled bills.
- Essential variable expenses are included in their appropriate forecast variant.
- Discretionary expenses remain estimates when projected.
- Gas expense assumptions adjust when vehicle unavailable.
- Transit fares only apply to actual trips.

## Strategies

- Transit-only works independently.
- Remote-only works independently.
- Hybrid works without overlapping wages or transit charges.
- Bill extension retains the liability.
- Subscription cancellation affects only relevant future charges.
- Alternative quotes only change price when confirmed.
- Assistance and borrowing affect the liability/cash ledger correctly when explicitly modeled.

## Ranking

- A $15 cancellation doesn't automatically outrank a high-impact, supported income-preservation strategy merely because of one slightly improved metric.
- Confirmed and conditional plans remain visibly distinct.
- Ranking is reproducible and justified.
- Plan diversity is preserved.
- No fabricated probabilities or benefits.

## Display

- Cash and outstanding liabilities aren't double-counted.
- Financial metrics use dollars.
- Earnings received versus earned are clear.
- Remaining bills are specifically identified.
- The expected benefit and limitations of each plan are understandable.

## Regression

All existing backend and frontend tests should continue passing.

Run integration tests for the default Maya scenario and at least one alternate scenario to ensure the accounting isn't hardcoded to the demo.

